This is the only local patch left in this port, and it is local on purpose:
it cannot be a reference, because no upstream revision of it exists.

upstream's qualcommax/patches-6.18/0950 (net: dsa: add out-of-band tagging
protocol, Maxime Chevallier) anchors its include/net/dsa.h hunk on

    #define DSA_TAG_PROTO_MXL862_8021Q_VALUE	31

which mainline 6.18.49 does not have - MXL862 DSA tags landed after 6.18. So
every revision of that patch fails here, and re-anchoring the same added
lines (the value-32 define and the enum member) after
DSA_TAG_PROTO_VSC73XX_8021Q_VALUE is the only way to land them. The added
lines are upstream's; the anchors are ours. That difference is exactly what
makes this a file to commit rather than a URL to fetch - and openwrt master's
copy of 0950 differs from the pinned one only in two hunk line numbers, so it
fails in the same place.

Same story in net/core/skbuff.c: 0950's include hunk fails on context, while
its sibling hunk (SKB_EXT_DSA_OOB) does apply and names struct
dsa_oob_tag_info, so the include has to come in with it.

The last hunk is not from 0950 at all: QCOM_EDMA has to select PAGE_POOL,
because qca_edma.c allocates its RX buffers with the page pool API and
mainline declares PAGE_POOL as

    config PAGE_POOL
	bool

with no prompt. A promptless symbol cannot be set from .config - kconfig only
consults the user value when the symbol is visible (sym_calc_value() in
scripts/kconfig/symbol.c) - so a "PAGE_POOL = y" line in the kernel config
would be silently discarded at olddefconfig time. select is the only way.
Upstream does not need this because their qualcommax config-6.18 ends up with
CONFIG_PAGE_POOL=y from something else they enable.

Deliberately NOT in here:

  - the guard that 737-02's last hunk puts around the PCS handover in
    phylink_major_config, even though that hunk does fail. The same patch's
    earlier hunks already applied the handover, and the guard tests
    mac_ops->mac_select_pcs - an op this stack never implements (the ipq6018
    PCS arrive through phylink's internal PCS list, via
    fwnode_phylink_pcs_parse in qca_ppe_main.c). Adding it would duplicate
    the two assignments and then skip them.

Everything else upstream wrote is fetched from the pin in ../../SOURCES.nix
and committed nowhere.
